## 5. Kubernetes Networking

Kubernetes networking provides communication between containers, Pods, Services and Nodes.

### Important Concepts

- Every Pod gets a unique IP address.
- Pods can communicate with each other.
- Containers inside the same Pod communicate through localhost.
- Services provide stable communication with Pods.
- CNI plugins implement Pod networking.

### Types of Kubernetes Communication

| Communication | Description |
|---|---|
| Container-to-Container | Communication inside the same Pod |
| Pod-to-Pod | Communication between Pods |
| Pod-to-Service | Communication using Service IP or DNS |
| External-to-Service | External access through Ingress, NodePort or LoadBalancer |

### CNI – Container Network Interface

CNI is responsible for implementing container networking.

Main responsibilities:

- Assigning Pod IP addresses.
- Configuring network routes.
- Providing Pod connectivity.
- Supporting communication across Nodes.

### Popular CNI Plugins

| Plugin | Main Feature |
|---|---|
| Calico | Network Policies |
| Flannel | Overlay Networking |
| Cilium | eBPF Networking |
| Weave | Container Networking |
| AWS VPC CNI | AWS VPC Networking |

Command:

```bash
kubectl get ds -A
```

This helps inspect DaemonSets running across namespaces.

