## 6. Container Runtime

Kubernetes uses the Container Runtime Interface (CRI) to communicate with container runtimes.

### Container Creation Flow

```text
kubectl
   |
Kubernetes API Server
   |
etcd
   |
Kubernetes Scheduler
   |
Kubelet
   |
CRI
   |
containerd
   |
containerd-shim
   |
runc
   |
Container Starts
```

### Important Components

| Component | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| API Server | Handles Kubernetes API requests |
| etcd | Stores cluster state |
| Scheduler | Selects a Node for the Pod |
| Kubelet | Manages Pods on a Node |
| CRI | Interface between kubelet and runtime |
| containerd | Manages container lifecycle |
| SHIM | Maintains container process management |
| runc | Starts the container process |

