## 7. Kubernetes Services

Pods are temporary. Their IP addresses can change when they are recreated.

A Kubernetes Service provides a stable IP address and DNS name to access backend Pods.

### Types of Services

| Service Type | Purpose |
|---|---|
| ClusterIP | Internal communication |
| NodePort | External access through Node IP |
| LoadBalancer | Cloud load balancer |
| ExternalName | DNS mapping |

### kube-proxy

kube-proxy runs on Nodes and manages Service networking.

Responsibilities:

- Service networking.
- Traffic forwarding.
- iptables/IPVS rules.
- Service virtual IP handling.

### CoreDNS

CoreDNS provides DNS-based Service Discovery inside Kubernetes.

Service DNS format:

```text
service-name.namespace.svc.cluster.local
```

Example:

```text
mysql.production.svc.cluster.local
```

Commands:

```bash
kubectl get pods -A

kubectl get svc

kubectl get pods -o wide

kubectl exec -it <pod-name> -- cat /etc/resolv.conf

kubectl exec -it <pod-name> -- nslookup <service-name>
```

### Service Discovery Example

```bash
kubectl exec -it <pod-name> -- curl nginx
```

Kubernetes resolves the Service name through CoreDNS.

